        <reference source="USN" ref_id="USN-8718-1" ref_url="https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8718-1" />
        <description>A flaw was found in SSSD. The extract_authtok_v1() function in the PAM responder does not validate the auth_token_length field against the remaining buffer size before processing. A local attacker can exploit this via a crafted protocol v1 request to the PAM responder socket, causing an out-of-bounds read and process crash, resulting in a denial of service.  Update Instructions:  Run `sudo pro fix CVE-2026-68743` to fix the vulnerability. The problem can be corrected by updating your system to the following package versions:  libipa-hbac0t64 - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libnss-sss - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libpam-sss - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libsss-certmap0 - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libsss-idmap0 - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libsss-nss-idmap0 - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 libsss-sudo - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 python3-libipa-hbac - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 python3-libsss-nss-idmap - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 python3-sss - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-ad - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-ad-common - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-common - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-dbus - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-idp - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-ipa - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-kcm - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-krb5 - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-krb5-common - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-ldap - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-passkey - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-proxy - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 sssd-tools - 2.12.0-1ubuntu5.4 No subscription required</description>
